# Stack and conventions

- Next.js 16 App Router with `cacheComponents` and `partialPrefetching` on. Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using an unfamiliar Next.js API.
- Request-time data (`cookies()`, `headers()`, session, DB reads per user) must render inside `<Suspense>`. Cacheable data uses `'use cache'`.
- TypeScript strict. Import app code via `@/` (maps to `src/`).
- Prisma 7: import the client from `@/generated/prisma/client`, never `@prisma/client`. Only `src/lib/db.ts` constructs `PrismaClient`.
- Server-only modules start with `import "server-only"`.
- Phaser 4 lives only under `src/game/phaser/` and is loaded with dynamic `import("phaser")` inside a client effect. Phaser's own agent docs are in `node_modules/phaser/skills/`.
- Game rules and scoring live in `src/game/engine/` and must not import React, Next.js, or Phaser.
- Validate all external input (forms, JSON, env vars) with Zod.
- Logging: use `logger` from `@/lib/logger`. Never `console.log` in committed server code.
- Package manager is pnpm. Do not add npm or yarn lockfiles.

```ts
// Good
import { prisma } from "@/lib/db";
// Bad
import { PrismaClient } from "@prisma/client";
```
